Not according to this spoiler:

http://nh.gmuf.com/wish.html#SECTION00030000000000000000

You get a 4/5 chance of getting +2, and a 3/5 chance of getting +3.  In
either case, if this chance fails you get +0.  

> At +3 there's a chance of getting a +0 but the chances end up with an
> average over 2,

You get an average of +1.8 if you wish for +3, and an average of +1.6 if
you wish for +2.

The odds for quantities of stackable items are slightly different (probably
to reflect the fact that if the chance fails, you get 1 instead of 0).

